 propellant","definition":"A propellant that is used to expel foods from an aerosol container.","id":78017,"biological_role":true},{"application":true,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:38867","name":"anaesthetic","definition":"Substance which produces loss of feeling or sensation.","id":38867,"biological_role":false},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:48706","name":"antagonist","definition":"Substance that attaches to and blocks cell receptors that normally bind naturally occurring substances.","id":48706,"biological_role":true},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:76971","name":"Escherichia coli metabolite","definition":"Any bacterial metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in <em>Escherichia coli</em>.","id":76971,"biological_role":true},{"application":true,"chemical_role":true,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:77974","name":"food packaging gas","definition":"A food additive that is a (generally inert) gas which is used to envelop foodstuffs during packing and so protect them from unwanted chemical reactions such as food spoilage or oxidation during subsequent transport and storage. The term includes propellant gases, used to expel foods from a container.","id":77974,"biological_role":true},{"application":true,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:50857","name":"anti-allergic agent","definition":"A drug used to treat allergic reactions.","id":50857,"biological_role":false},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:75772","name":"Saccharomyces cerevisiae metabolite","definition":"Any  fungal metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in Baker's yeast (<em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae </em>).","id":75772,"biological_role":true},{"application":true,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:35480","name":"analgesic","definition":"An agent capable of relieving pain without the loss of consciousness or without producing anaesthesia. In addition, analgesic is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to cause a reduction of pain symptoms.","id":35480,"biological_role":true}],"is_released":true}